+## Decisions and remaining limits
+
+No spec or engine-wording decision was needed. When the reached turn is filtered out, its marker is placed before the visible subset because the filter intentionally omits turns; the model and delivery state remain unchanged. The filtered list can contain turns from different positions relative to the marker, so the marker describes the side's reached position, not a claim that every visible filtered turn follows it chronologically.
+
+The independent follow-up review found the hidden-turn fallback lacked the same visual connector. I extracted a shared reached-note group, so both inline markers and markers above a filtered/folded-out turn use the short inset rail; it remains above the visible subset rather than being assigned to a different turn. Review follow-up found no remaining concern in the marker placement or accessibility structure.
